## 2. Inter-Process Communication (IPC) & Zero-Copy Data Layer

To make 5 languages act like a single binary on Windows 11 with sub-millisecond latency, **JSON serialization over HTTP is strictly avoided** for data payloads.

* **Control Plane (Commands & Events):** **gRPC over Windows Named Pipes** (`\\.\pipe\fpa_control_bus`). Protobuf schemas strictly type all contracts across Rust, Go, Elixir, and Java.
* **Data Plane (Large Matrices & Datasets):** **Apache Arrow in Windows Shared Memory (Memory-Mapped Files)**.
  * *Example Flow:* Go ingests a 2GB CSV -> writes directly into an Apache Arrow record batch in Windows Shared Memory -> passes the memory pointer via Named Pipe to Rust -> Rust reads the matrix with **zero serialization/deserialization overhead** -> Java reads the same memory pointer to export a formatted Excel report.

