## 6. Offline-First Architecture & Local AI Copilot

### 6.1 Storage & Local Version Control
* **Primary Analytical Store:** **DuckDB** (embedded in Rust) stores historical actuals, general ledger transactions, and dense historical cubes in highly compressed columnar format.
* **Metadata & Graph Store:** **SQLite** (with **SQLCipher** AES-256 encryption) stores model structure, user permissions, dimension hierarchies, formulas, workflow states, and audit logs.
* **Project File Format (`.fpa`):** A single portable archive or workspace directory backed by **Git-like content-addressable storage** (managed by the Go daemon). Users can save checkpoints, revert to any point in time offline, or send an encrypted `.fpa` file to a colleague.

### 6.2 Offline-to-Online Synchronization (When Connected)
* **Solo Offline Mode:** Zero external dependencies. Runs indefinitely on an air-gapped Windows 11 laptop.
* **LAN Peer-to-Peer Mode:** In secure corporate environments without cloud access, the Go daemon uses **mDNS** and **TLS over TCP** to allow multiple analysts on the same local network to collaborate in real time via **CRDTs (Conflict-Free Replicated Data Types)** and Elixir’s distributed OTP cluster.
* **Hybrid Cloud Sync:** When internet connectivity is detected (and if configured), the Go daemon performs delta-compressed, end-to-end encrypted synchronization with a remote server or S3-compatible object store.

### 6.3 100% Offline Local AI FP&A Copilot
* **Engine:** Rust hosts the **ONNX Runtime** connected to **Windows 11 DirectML**, executing a quantized local Small Language Model (e.g., *Phi-4-Mini* or *Qwen-2.5-Coder-7B-Instruct* at 4-bit quantization, requiring ~4GB VRAM/RAM).
* **Capabilities (No data ever leaves the laptop):**
  1. **Natural Language to Formula:** User types *"Calculate 3-month rolling average of Gross Margin excluding APAC"* -> AI generates exact Hyperblock DSL syntax.
  2. **Automated Flux Commentary:** Reads the variance table in DuckDB and drafts MD&A executive commentary explaining *why* EBITDA missed budget by $1.2M (tracing the DAG down to specific cost centers and GL accounts).
  3. **Anomaly Detection:** Local Isolation Forest / Prophet time-series models (in Rust) flag unusual GL entries or broken forecast trends during data import.

